{"agent":"plock2g","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`real_overlap` tests whether any `p` in `real` matches glob `a` (the caller's own glob, `mine`), rather than matching glob `b` (the holder's declared claim glob, `theirs`). Given `mine = [\"a/x.py\"]`, `theirs = [\"b/**\"]`, and `changed = [\"a/x.py\"]`, `conflicts(mine, theirs)` yields an empty list so `pairs` is empty and the function returns `[]`. But if `mine` and `theirs` structurally overlap by prefix (e.g., `mine = [\"a/**\"]`, `theirs = [\"a/**\"]`), but `real` only contains a file that matches `mine` and not `b`, the condition `any(glob_match(p, a) for p in real)` incorrectly checks if the holder's changed files match *our* glob `a` instead of checking if they match *their* glob `b`.","digest":"d0c99bf477315af0","family":"google","location":"ddflow/core/admission.py:91","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/admission.py:91"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`real_overlap` keeps a wildcard pair when any changed path matches the claimant glob `a`, and never checks that path against the holder glob `b`. Given `mine=[\"src/**\"]`, `theirs=[\"src/pkg/**\"]`, `changed=[\"src/other.py\"]`, prefix `conflicts` still emits `(\"src/**\", \"src/pkg/**\")` and `glob_match(\"src/other.py\", \"src/**\")` is true, so the pair is kept even though the holder never touched `src/pkg/`. Those claims are disjoint and should run in parallel; the tests only cover a narrower claimant (`a/x.py` vs `a/**`), which hides this.","digest":"b354ad5c78d8224b","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/core/admission.py:95","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/admission.py:95"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6063,"diff_sha":"794ff24a9d24d5dcbee261ab91fefadd3e11295f70671913d57a73214527eac7","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-lease-real-overlap","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":194.5,"family":"google","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"55f770d1bed4b2a6","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-lease-real-overlap.critic.grok-4.7.20261110T145328Z-1dba0aa3.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"bd7cc1e0ee2cc9b14f0e0ecb53ba445480baba15","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/core/admission.py":"100644 be39fc6713840f12ca760f8d10456e46846c5e94","ddflow/services/leases/common.py":"100644 6219d1b9c2f87f4c147bef9068dbb60e14463cdc","tests/test_lease_real_overlap.py":"100644 7bf39fa8cb18afabce1dcaff031c2400c50734ff"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/admission.py:91","ddflow/core/admission.py:95"],"tree_sha":"bd7cc1e0ee2c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e84a23a17df25b9baf37ce644","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":166935,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-lease-real-overlap","ts":"2026-11-10T14:56:43.058677Z"}
